568 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(The changed workload is 55,000 sender tracking look-ups per hour, while reconciled handover corrections are committed every six hours. The average request rate is 55,000 / 3,600 = 15.28 look-ups per second. This is an average planning rate, not a peak rate or measured server throughput. The read workload is now explicitly frequent and the correction workload is periodic. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

569 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(A controlled read projection may be acceptable if it is derived from the BCNF source, has a defined snapshot boundary, and is refreshed atomically after each reconciled correction batch. It must be treated as a read model, not a second independent source of truth. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

570 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(CSA05 DBMS \205 CO2 Assignment Answers | Page 14 )/Pg 23 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

571 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(Recommended logical source of truth: the BCNF design. It directly represents the declared determinants, avoids repeated sender/service/operator/policy facts, supports restrictive referential integrity, and preserves the stated dependencies in the corresponding relations. It also makes catalog and coordinator amendments local to their determinant rows. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

572 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(The recommendation is based on correctness and update behavior implied by the rules, not on fabricated performance results. Before final submission, cite the actual Task 9 measurements. If the benchmark demonstrates that the read path is too expensive for the operational workload, retain the BCNF source schema and add a controlled read projection rather than permanently duplicating the authoritative source data. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

573 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(The costs are additional joins for expanded reads, more relations to administer, and policy-version considerations if policy mappings change over time. Derived fields should not be stored redundantly unless there is a documented refresh and validation process. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

574 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(Interpretation should be tied to actual recorded values. The theoretical expectation is that the flat design needs many repeated-row updates for catalog and operator facts; the partial design removes sender and service-description updates from the observation rows but still repeats assignment and policy facts; the BCNF design changes a catalog or coordinator fact in its determinant relation once. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

575 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(The normalized query may require additional joins to expand a full handover record. Whether those joins are slower depends on indexes, selectivity, cache state, row width, optimizer choices and the in-memory/storage engine. A local benchmark can compare the tested workload on the tested machine; it cannot establish production throughput or guarantee that 55,000 requests per hour will be served under different concurrency, network, hardware or data- distribution conditions. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

576 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(Insert measured timings and storage numbers from Task 9 before making any claim that one design was faster or smaller. Explain exceptions\204for example, a narrow normalized table may reduce I/O, while extra joins may add CPU work. )/Pg 23 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

