<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(May expand joins on each lookup; optimizer behavior must be measured. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

600 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Uses extra storage; requires atomic refresh, version/snapshot control and validation. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

601 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(High risk of drift, duplicate updates and inconsistent copies; not recommended as an independent authoritative store. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

602 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(AMySQL ordinary view is not itself a materialized view. A read card can be implemented as a physical table maintained transactionally by the application or a controlled stored procedure/job. The local benchmark must compare the ordinary normalized join path with indexed card look-ups and measure refresh cost. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

603 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(The hourly demand corresponds to approximately 15.28 average look-ups per second. That demand justifies testing an indexed read projection, but it does not by itself prove that normalization is inadequate. The BCNF dependencies remain valid because a read projection does not alter the logical source rules. The six-hour correction cadence offers a natural refresh boundary, provided the business accepts the resulting snapshot timing and the refresh is atomic. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

604 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Final defence: retain BCNF as the authoritative transactional schema and modify the physical read path with a validated, indexed tracking projection if the measured query and refresh results justify its storage and maintenance cost. If the actual benchmark shows the normalized query already meets the service target, retain the BCNF read path and avoid unnecessary duplication. This conditional decision is more defensible than inventing a performance result. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

605 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Decision: MODIFY, not replace, the logical BCNF source schema. Add a sender tracking read card containing only the fields required by the tracking response\204for example, SenderID, ServiceID, DispatchWave, Completion, ServiceBand, RouteFactor and any sender-facing display fields actually required. Add a composite index beginning with the lookup predicates, such as \(SenderID, DispatchWave, ServiceID\), after confirming the real query pattern. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

606 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Refresh protocol: process the six-hour correction batch in one transaction or versioned staging workflow; rebuild/update affected read-card rows; validate row counts and key uniqueness; compare a sample or full checksum against the source query; publish the new version atomically; retain the prior version until readers no longer need it. Readers must see one consistent version, not a mixture of pre- and post-correction rows. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

607 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Storage and update consequences must be quantified from the actual generated dataset. The additional allocated bytes equal the read-card table plus its indexes; the extra writes equal the inserted/updated/deleted card rows during refresh. Do not claim numerical values until measured. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

